<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Callaeci</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The hillfort peoples of north-western Iberia, whose castro culture shaped Galicia and northern Portugal and who held out against Rome until 19 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Callaeci, or Gallaeci, occupied the north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia-and-lodomeria">Galicia</a> and northern Portugal. Their culture grew from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> castro culture, marked by hundreds of fortified hilltop settlements of round stone houses.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were divided into many small communities rather than one state, each based on a castro such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/citania-de-briteiros">Citânia de Briteiros</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castro-of-santa-trega">Santa Tecla</a>. They mined gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a>, worked bronze and gold into torcs, and built sauna-like bathhouses with carved stones. They spoke a Celtic language, worshipped gods such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandua">Bandua</a>, and erected stone warrior statues.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decimus-junius-brutus-callaicus">Decimus Junius Brutus</a> campaigned among them in 137 BCE and took the name Callaicus, but conquest was completed only in Augustus' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a>, ending in 19 BCE. Their land became the Roman region and later province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gallaecia">Gallaecia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg>